    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d294">

                <pb facs="0395" n="383" xml:id="pg383"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">852.00/6358</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Chief of the Division of American
                        Republics</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Duggan</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >of a Conversation With the Brazilian Ambassador</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Aranha</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-09-01">September 1, 1937</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The Brazilian Ambassador stated that his Government desired to act in concert
                    with the United States with regard to the Uruguayan proposal that a state of
                    belligerency be recognized in Spain. I informed the Ambassador in general of the
                    nature of our proposed reply, which he said he would transmit at once to his
                    Government with a strong plea that it adopt the same attitude. The Ambassador
                    assured me that he would have the reply by tomorrow, and expressed the hope that
                    this Government might see fit to hold up its note to the Uruguayans until he had
                    word that the substance of the two replies would be in agreement.</p>
            </div>
